# Placeholder ensuring e2e/storage-states/ directory exists in git.
#
# This directory holds Playwright `storageState` JSON files that cache
# authenticated browser context (cookies, localStorage, sessionStorage)
# per role. The JSON files are:
#   - Generated at suite startup by e2e/global-setup.ts (or via
#     `npm run e2e:generate-storage-states`).
#   - Consumed by e2e/fixtures/auth.fixture.ts to skip per-test login.
#   - Gitignored (per `.gitignore` rule `e2e/storage-states/*.json`).
#   - Reset on every CI run; preserved locally for fast iteration.
#
# Per-role files (each generated only if the corresponding env vars are set):
#   - canonical-user.json   (default authenticated user)
#   - admin-user.json       (admin role)
#   - viewer-user.json      (read-only viewer role)
#   - restricted-user.json  (under-privileged user for denial-path tests)
#
# References:
#   - AAP §0.4.4 (Test Data and Fixtures Design)
#   - AAP §0.5.1.2 (.gitkeep placeholder requirement)
#   - AAP §0.10.2 (Storage state lifecycle)
#   - e2e/global-setup.ts (generation logic)
#   - e2e/global-teardown.ts (cleanup logic)
#   - e2e/fixtures/auth.fixture.ts (consumption logic)
